<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Massana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Massana is one of the seven parishes of Andorra and the name of its main town, in the north-west of the principality on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valira">Valira</a> del Nord. It includes the villages of Arinsal and Pal, whose ski slopes form the Vallnord area, and the Comapedrosa, at 2,942 metres the highest peak of Andorra.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-massana.jpg" alt="La Massana" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jlmoncada · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LaMassana_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
